    {
      "mentions": [],
      "body": "The added cell's logic runs cleanly against synthetic data (I verified this offline since the sandbox's S3 access to the actual validation data is stalled/unavailable, so I couldn't drive the notebook's own inference cell to completion \u2014 I interrupted that hung run rather than let it sit indefinitely).\n\n**Change made:** `4_confusion_matrix.ipynb` previously ended after a markdown cell describing the confusion matrix step but had no code to actually compute it. I added a final code cell that:\n- Thresholds `y_prob` (already computed by the notebook's inference cell) at `THRESHOLD = 0.5`, matching the `BinaryAccuracy(threshold=0.5)` used elsewhere in this app's metrics.\n- Prints accuracy and a full `classification_report` (precision/recall/F1 per class, labeled \"No event\"/\"Event\").\n- Builds and plots a `ConfusionMatrixDisplay` from `confusion_matrix(y_true, y_pred)`.\n\nIt reuses `confusion_matrix`, `classification_report`, `ConfusionMatrixDisplay`, and `plt`, which the notebook's first cell already imports, and it doesn't touch any of the earlier cells.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: this sandbox appears to have no (or a very slow) path to the `s3://nasa-surya-bench` bucket the dataset reads from \u2014 the validation dataloader stalled for 7+ minutes on a single file read with zero GPU utilization. I couldn't get an end-to-end run with real numbers here; you'll want to run this notebook yourself where S3 access works to confirm the actual confusion matrix.",
      "id": "50176744-16e9-4233-a0ca-a129630db9c7",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
